{"step_index":384,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T06:53:23Z","content":"Here is the complete recap of our session and the onboarding journey:\n\n---\n\n# 📋 Master Recap: Server Onboarding & IaC Mastery\n\n### 1. Persona & Tooling Integration\n* **`koby-bowser-sysadmin`**: Adopted and permanently registered the Claude Code sysadmin persona into Antigravity as a global skill ([`~/.gemini/config/skills/koby-bowser-sysadmin/SKILL.md`](file:///home/koby/.gemini/config/skills/koby-bowser-sysadmin/SKILL.md)) and an active subagent.\n* **Semaphore Integration**: Configured the Semaphore MCP server in [`~/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json`](file:///home/koby/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json) and verified direct API authentication (<span style=\"color:green\">**200 OK**</span>) against `https://semaphore.corp.intranet.local`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Target Investigation: `mtq-mailsrvp-01`\nWe investigated the Martinique production mail server (`172.30.39.153:30`):\n* **Stack**: Debian 13 (Trixie), running **Postfix** (SMTP:25), **Dovecot** (IMAP/POP3), **Nginx** (Roundcube webmail), and local MariaDB.\n* **TLS Material**: Verified that the Let's Encrypt certificate for `postfix.outremer-telecom.fr` was active and valid until Nov 15, 2026.\n* **Initial State**: Noted as *\"hors IaC\"* (unmanaged by Ansible), but had `spui-runner` already created with the PROD runner key.\n\n---\n\n### 3. The DEV Zone Attempt & Firewall Reality Check\n* **Goal**: You requested onboarding `mtq-mailsrvp-01` into the **DEV** inventory.\n* **Action**:\n  * You appended the DEV runner key (`semaphore-runner`) to `/etc/ssh/authorized_keys/spui-runner`.\n  * We created branch `feat/onboard-mtq-mailsrvp-dev`, added the host to [`inventories/dev/hosts.yml`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/inventories/dev/hosts.yml), generated **MR !266**, and merged it.\n  * Created Template `130` on Semaphore and triggered **Task #914**.\n* **The Diagnostic Catch**:\n  * Task #914 failed with <span style=\"color:red\">**`ssh: connect to host 172.30.39.153 port 30: Operation timed out`**</span>.\n  * **Root Cause Identified**: The host firewall was open, but the corporate **inter-VLAN firewall strictly blocks the DEV runner** (`th2-ansid-run1` in `172.30.242.x`) from routing into the Martinique PROD subnet (`172.30.39.0/24`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Moving to PROD & Total Victory\n* **Realignment**:\n  * Created branch `feat/move-mtq-mailsrvp-to-prod`.\n  * Removed `mtq-mailsrvp-01` from DEV and added it to [`inventories/prod/hosts.yml`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/inventories/prod/hosts.yml) under an isolated `mail_servers` group (ensuring standard web/db playbooks never touch it).\n  * Auto-created **MR !267** in one shot via git push options (`-o merge_request.create`), which was approved and merged into `main`.\n* **The Live Semaphore Test**:\n  * Created Template `131` (*`Check Linux Distro and Kernel - PROD (recon)`*).\n  * Triggered **Task #915** with `--limit mtq-mailsrvp-01` dispatched to the **PROD runner** (**`th2-ansip-run1`**).\n  * **Result**: Finished in **7 seconds flat** with <span style=\"color:green\">**SUCCESS**</span>! \n  * `mtq-mailsrvp-01` reported <span style=\"color:green\">**ONLINE**</span> on Debian 13.6 (Kernel `6.12.95+deb13-amd64`).\n\n---\n\n### 5. Codified into Permanent Memory\nTo ensure we execute future server onboardings in minutes without re-learning the pitfalls:\n* Documented the complete 5-step Standard Operating Procedure directly in [`~/.gemini/config/AGENTS.md`](file:///home/koby/.gemini/config/AGENTS.md) (network reality check, `spui-runner` key setup, surgical inventory declaration, one-shot GitLab MR push, and fast Semaphore verification).\n\n---\n\nEverything in the repo is clean, fast-forwarded to `origin/main` at `81767ed`, and ready for our next mission!","thinking":"**Recalling agent integration process**\n\nInitial integration involved adapting a sysadmin agent definition from an external code platform. Registration occurred within the Antigravity system as a global skill accessible through a specific invocation syntax. This adaptation marked the initial onboarding step for the external agent.\n\n\n**Assessing initial infrastructure landscape**\n\nThe system's infrastructure management resides within a specific code repository, organized across multiple environments including 'dev', 'val', 'corp', and 'prod'. Strict \"hard production safety rules\" must be adhered to in the production environment. A central configuration file governs access to the infrastructure management control plane.\n\nThe target mail server, 'mtq-mailsrvp-01', appears accessible with identified services. The server already has an existing runner, initially configured only for the production environment. Now, attempting onboarding into the development zone requires adding a development runner key to the mail server.\n\n\n"}
