{"step_index":437,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-17T11:37:50Z","thinking":"Initial hypothesis involves creating a Python or Ansible script to extract domains and certificate paths from Nginx and Apache configurations. A key consideration is the potential for an inline Python script using a standard Python runtime. The effectiveness of this approach needs evaluation.\n\n\nNginx configuration extraction can begin by parsing the output of a validation command, or alternatively, by directly inspecting configuration files in specific directories. The primary indicators of interest within `server` blocks are the domain names, certificate paths, and listener configurations.\n\nApache virtual hosts can be obtained using a status command that outputs virtual host configurations, including domain names and associated configuration file locations, enabling extraction of SSL certificate paths.\n\n\nA Python script executed remotely appears to be the most robust approach; it will check the status of web servers and extract relevant configuration data. The script will handle cases where a server is inactive or not installed, providing appropriate reporting. Testing with a known system (`mtq-mailsrvp-01`) will validate the extraction logic, particularly the certificate data acquisition.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python3 -c '\\nimport re\\n\\nnginx_sample = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\nserver {\\n    listen 80;\\n    server_name example.com www.example.com;\\n    return 301 https://$host$request_uri;\\n}\\n\\nserver {\\n    listen 443 ssl http2;\\n    server_name example.com www.example.com;\\n\\n    ssl_certificate /etc/ssl/certs/example.crt;\\n    ssl_certificate_key /etc/ssl/private/example.key;\\n\\n    location / {\\n        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8080;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\ndef parse_nginx_conf(text):\\n    servers = []\\n    # Match server blocks (handling braces)\\n    # A simple tokenizer/parser for server blocks:\\n    blocks = re.findall(r\\\"server\\\\s*\\\\{([^\\\\{\\\\}]*(?:\\\\{[^\\\\{\\\\}]*\\\\}[^\\\\{\\\\}]*)*)\\\\}\\\", text, re.DOTALL)\\n    for b in blocks:\\n        names = re.findall(r\\\"server_name\\\\s+([^;]+);\\\", b)\\n        certs = re.findall(r\\\"ssl_certificate\\\\s+([^;]+);\\\", b)\\n        keys = re.findall(r\\\"ssl_certificate_key\\\\s+([^;]+);\\\", b)\\n        ports = re.findall(r\\\"listen\\\\s+([^;]+);\\\", b)\\n        \\n        parsed_names = []\\n        for n in names:\\n            parsed_names.extend(n.split())\\n            \\n        ssl_cert = certs[0].strip() if certs else None\\n        ssl_key = keys[0].strip() if keys else None\\n        \\n        servers.append({\\n            \\\"domains\\\": parsed_names,\\n            \\\"ports\\\": [p.strip() for p in ports],\\n            \\\"ssl_certificate\\\": ssl_cert,\\n            \\\"ssl_key\\\": ssl_key\\n        })\\n    return servers\\n\\nprint(parse_nginx_conf(nginx_sample))\\n'\"","Cwd":"\"/home/koby\"","RunPersistent":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"3000","toolAction":"\"Running command\"","toolSummary":"\"Test nginx parser in python\""}}]}
